A. null contraction of the xi-coupled scalar stress tensor (flat)
  [ok] k k T = (k.dphi)^2 - xi (k.d)^2 phi^2 
     => along x = lambda k the xi-term is d^2/dlambda^2 of <phi^2>; it integrates to a boundary term, so ANEC is xi-independent in flat space
B. finite-mode model: 4D Minkowski massless scalar on a null line
     L =   0.5   <0|Q_L|0> = +0.000e+00   min spec Q_L = -3.198409e-01
     L =   1.0   <0|Q_L|0> = +0.000e+00   min spec Q_L = -2.150653e-01
     L =   2.0   <0|Q_L|0> = +0.000e+00   min spec Q_L = -1.720874e-02
     L =   4.0   <0|Q_L|0> = +0.000e+00   min spec Q_L = -4.417916e-07
     L =   8.0   <0|Q_L|0> = +0.000e+00   min spec Q_L = -3.666617e-27
     L =  16.0   <0|Q_L|0> = +0.000e+00   min spec Q_L = -6.099107e-108
     L =  32.0   <0|Q_L|0> = +0.000e+00   min spec Q_L = +0.000000e+00
  [ok] vacuum expectation is exactly 0 at every L (saturation) 
  [ok] finite window: spectrum dips below 0 (no null QI on a segment) 
  [ok] min spec -> 0^- as L grows (ANEC >= 0 over the complete line) 
     u = l.k per mode: [0.6969 0.8643 2.4892]
C. Fewster-Roman explicit states obey ANEC (gr-qc/0209036 eqs II.24,II.37-38)
     double integral = Lambda0**3*f0/(630*pi)
     ANEC(alpha)     = 4*Lambda0**3*alpha**(2*sigma - 7)*f0/(315*pi*(alpha**(2*sigma - 6) + 128*pi**4))
  [ok] double integral = 2 pi f0 C * 2 L0^7/105 
     sigma=3.75, L0=f(0)=1: ANEC(0.2) = 1.4498e-07   ANEC(0.005) = 2.2923e-08
  [ok] ANEC value > 0 and decreasing to 0 as alpha -> 0 
  [ok] segment average exponent sigma - 4 < 0 (rho_2 -> -inf) and 2sigma-7 > 0 
D. Urban-Olum anomalous ANEC violation, conformally flat 4D (0910.5925 Sec.III)
  [ok] eq.(39): box omega = 2 r^-2 (b-2a) e^{-v^2/r^2} 
  [ok] eq.(40): omega_,vv = 2a r^-2 (2v^2/r^2 - 1) e^{-v^2/r^2} 
  [ok] eq.(41) reproduced from (38) 
  [ok] eq.(42): int T_vv dv = (ab - 2a^2) 16 beta sqrt(2 pi)/r^3 
     a=0.01, b=0.05, r=1: ANEC integral = -2.1165e-07 (vacuum state, test field)
  [ok] negative for b > 2a: ANEC fails in a curved (conformally flat) background 
RESULT: ALL AGREE
